invariant: INV-17
file: src/aead_avx512.c
catches: test/avx512-run.sh bin/aead_avx512_equiv_test
builds: bin/aead_avx512_equiv_test
reason: hash_rest returns without wiping the struct of powers, r^2 to r^16, so
  the entries' dead frames keep them. r and a tag seen on the wire give
  the pad, and r and the pad forge any message under that key. Every tag
  is still right. bin/aead_avx512_equiv_test copies the stack below each
  entry and looks for the powers. It needs a CPU with AVX-512 IFMA, or
  Intel SDE through SDE64; without either this reports unguarded rather
  than caught.

--- old
    ct_wipe(of_r, sizeof *of_r);
--- new
    (void)of_r;
